A||||8||86SE||Who has their subs mounted in the front compartment????||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||05-01-2000||07:18 PM||||How does it sound up there and what are the sizes of boxes you use??<P>Are there any other places to put a 10" sub in a Fiero to get some good bass from an 800 watt amp??||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||05-01-2000||09:08 PM||||I'm gonna try to put some subs behind the seats.. it's been done before, the only concern I have is retaining full seat movement.. sometimes being tall sucks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||05-01-2000||09:20 PM||||Hehe, I just got finished playing with my stereo with my 10" sub.<P>I got a Polk Audio db series sub, meant for small spaces and hard bass.<P>I tried it behind the seat, woofer facing my back.  Sounded and felt GREAT, but the passenger got nill.  So I figured if the bass is facing right to me only, it must sound like crap.  So I moved it to the front, woofer facing the hood.<P>It sounded mediocre, very little bass and it just rattled the hood.  I then turned it around to face the tub.  It sounded better, but it still felt mediocre.  <P>So since I am not the TALLEST person in the world, I put it back into the seat, this time facing the firewall.  People told me it would sound crappy because the firewall would soak up the waves.  But it sounds GREAT!<P>The bass carries all throughout the car, and the passenger and driver feels it all equally!<P>Plus, I mounted the speaker higher towards the top of the seat and it just rattles everything.  <P>I say, if you aren't too tall, drop it behind the seat.<P>WARNING:  Everything feels really good when sitting, but after each new placement, start the car and take it around the block.  Everything changes when you have to feel it above the engine vibrations.  That's the absolute reason the front trunk sucked.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||05-01-2000||09:29 PM||||BTW, my speaker has a custome box that is around 14" W X 14" L X 8" H.<P>What sub do you have?  An 800W amp seems extreme for one 10" sub.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||05-01-2000||09:52 PM||||My father let me have his home theatre subwoofer box. I removed the home speaker and put in a "12 dual voice coil speaker. Fits perfectly on the passenger side floor flush with the seat and easy to remove. My wife loves it cause she says I can't pick up any blonde hitchikers <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> It cranks, ask Cobra!||||reg||14
Z||000005||fierosound||05-01-2000||10:29 PM||||You may want to check out this website, he has subs in the front compartment.<BR> <A HREF="http://geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/fss.html" TARGET=_blank>http://geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/fss.html</A> <P><BR>Also, as you may know, I have a 10" sub behind each seat, running only 50 watts to each!  But it still gets VERY LOW and LOUD!  Wish I had 100 watts to each though...  <P>One of the determining factors to be mindful of is the speaker's efficiency rating and frequency response.  The OZ Audios 10" 250L subs have a rating of 93db and range of 19hz-2000hz in a small box.  Many competitive subs have ratings of 89db or less and can't reproduce frequencies lower that 25-30hz!  A low efficiency speaker NEEDS more power.  One short on lows sometimes needs a huge box to compensate so it can give you that low bass.  Choose your subs carefully.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||phillip||05-02-2000||08:33 AM||||i have 1 jl audio 8" in a wood/fiberglass enclosure in the passenger side footwell. no one complains about lack of foot room and it sounds pretty good. i'm hoping to change to power windows so i can put 8's in the doors too. i've done it in a blazer and i think i can get them enough air and keep them sealed. then i'll try 3 jl 8w0 12 0hms.||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||05-02-2000||08:55 AM||||Thanks for all the replys!!<P>By the way, it is a Petras Hyper-Throw 10" competition sub, 500-700watt power handling.<P>Now im thinking about mounting it either in the passenger foot well, or behind the drives seat.||||reg||10
Z||000008||IiplayaziI||05-02-2000||09:54 PM||||I met fierosound the other day and I say his subs rock.. he should almost sell the specs for the boxes. Its a must do for subs. I can see it right now.. two 10s in the back out of the way and 2 8's in the door.. WHAT I CANT HEAR YOU  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Ive seen and heard subs in the front and even in the spare compartment. I recommend boxes in the back.||||reg||1
